{"id": "EUVD-2026-76465", "enisaUuid": "e9db1f44-1d1f-3f71-a411-9957a2bf89d1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmptcp: fix uninitialized local_id in syncookie MP_JOIN reconstruction\n\nmptcp_token_join_cookie_init_state() restores remote_nonce, local_nonce,\nbackup, join_id, token and msk from the saved cookie entry when rebuilding\nthe request socket for a MP_JOIN 4th-ACK handled under SYN cookies, but it\ndoes not restore local_id, even though the SYN path saved it.\nsubflow_ulp_clone() then reads that uninitialized field and stores it as\nthe joined subflow's address-ID. Because the request-sock slab is\nSLAB_TYPESAFE_BY_RCU and not zeroed on allocation, the value is the stale\nbyte of a previously freed request socket, which an off-path peer can\ninfluence by sending concurrent MP_JOIN SYNs. This corrupts the path\nmanager's id-based subflow bookkeeping for the connection.\n\nRestore subflow_req->local_id from the cookie entry, as done for the other\nfields.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:48:47", "baseScore": 8.2, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4534e0eead692bb069ad1e6a5a245fc2e2078300", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63cacb05e51a1c6e1349d2e593d00fd6ef43def4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/954b5ea836eb118d188975ced803448537ab8479", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9df36a4846375a9b75bf42d77bfed216b0f366f9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64f2c5dd49b956a542c8c02b8dad5d262a462bba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51887ccd88791ddaa8755a7c614fda031ecf7982", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf19d166337c6488b39cb03eeeffb30a941d6326", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b878dfdd12d7a5b8722a78d35e313506140ca3d9"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9vj3-qjq5-h6jg", "CVE-2026-89554"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.6, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a0fefe2-02bf-392a-bc5e-b6a4d9f569d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.9"}, {"id": "1d003666-ca59-3bf1-9a7f-9c1db35b7625", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9466a1ccebbe54ac57fb8a89c2b4b854826546a8 <4534e0eead692bb069ad1e6a5a245fc2e2078300"}, {"id": "2691d7cd-c32c-330d-b198-427869d8130c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9466a1ccebbe54ac57fb8a89c2b4b854826546a8 <9df36a4846375a9b75bf42d77bfed216b0f366f9"}, {"id": "293a808e-ab17-3d0c-b336-2eb5d3574a2c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "302d1d9e-a6a4-3e79-b45f-0c94726c2778", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9466a1ccebbe54ac57fb8a89c2b4b854826546a8 <64f2c5dd49b956a542c8c02b8dad5d262a462bba"}, {"id": "305c84e1-d51c-3039-a080-c9598626b3ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9466a1ccebbe54ac57fb8a89c2b4b854826546a8 <bf19d166337c6488b39cb03eeeffb30a941d6326"}, {"id": "574e9076-9356-3167-b6ea-033f333d21d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "5e9f795e-8537-3782-bfe9-97a9f74b8f19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "5f7cd99f-0002-32ce-955c-9683f84d8487", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "640e7769-9def-341e-bb2d-2c984fc9ed78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9466a1ccebbe54ac57fb8a89c2b4b854826546a8 <b878dfdd12d7a5b8722a78d35e313506140ca3d9"}, {"id": "7fa07e52-7a48-3a27-b7c8-51b3f4298143", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9466a1ccebbe54ac57fb8a89c2b4b854826546a8 <954b5ea836eb118d188975ced803448537ab8479"}, {"id": "8fe5d6c7-ef0a-3b52-b131-3a5f4c12e6d6", "product": {"name